# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored -- keep it that way.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Everything ABOVE the line is an Edge Function secret, and the whole file
# can be pushed at once:
#
#   supabase secrets set --env-file .env
#
# Nothing below the line belongs in this file. Those values live in other
# files on other machines, and they are listed here so that one page shows
# every value the door opener needs.

# ── Edge Function secrets ─────────────────────────────────────

# The home controller's key. Accepted only by door-events, which is read
# only. Deliberately a different secret from the device key so the two
# rotate independently: this one leaks a list of times and labels, the
# other one is on a board screwed to a wall.
DOOR_DASHBOARD_KEY=

# The manager key. Accepted only by door-admin, which creates, edits and
# deletes passes. The most powerful of the three: it can mint a pass that
# opens the door. Whoever holds it can let anyone in, so treat handing it
# over as handing over a front door key.
#
#   node tools/make-key.js admin
#
# Used by tools/manage.html on a desktop and public/passes.html on a phone.
# Neither page stores it anywhere but the browser it was pasted into.
DOOR_ADMIN_KEY=

# Which origin the browser page is served from, for the CORS header on
# door-open. Leave empty to allow any origin, which is the shipped default
# because the Netlify URL is not known until the site exists. Fill it in
# once you have one:
#
#   DOOR_ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://your-site.netlify.app
#
# Left commented out deliberately. Pushing it empty would set the secret to
# an empty string rather than leaving it unset, which the function now
# treats as unset anyway, but there is no reason to store a blank.
# DOOR_ALLOWED_ORIGIN=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything below goes somewhere else. Listed so this file is the whole
# checklist.
#
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
#   Injected into the Edge Functions by Supabase. Nothing to set, and they
#   cannot be set here: the platform reserves the SUPABASE_ prefix.
#
# public/config.js            openUrl, adminUrl
#   https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co/functions/v1/door-open
#   https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co/functions/v1/door-admin
#   Both public. They are served to every visitor and that is fine: the
#   functions check a key, and the keys are not in this file's half of the
#   world.
#
# firmware/door_opener/config.h    (copy from config.h.example)
#   WIFI_SSID, WIFI_PASSWORD
#   DOOR_POLL_URL     https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co/rest/v1/rpc/door_claim
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY from Supabase Settings > API. Not a secret
#   DOOR_DEVICE_KEY   from `node tools/make-key.js device`. Its hash goes in
#                     the door_keys table, not here: the board is the only
#                     thing that ever holds the plaintext
#   RELAY_PIN, RELAY_ACTIVE_LOW
#   SUPABASE_ROOT_CA  paste the root certificate, see the comment there
#
# ../home-controller/.env     (the door panel and the bulb flash)
#   DOOR_EVENTS_URL      https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co/functions/v1/door-events
#   DOOR_DASHBOARD_KEY   the same value as above
#   DOOR_FLASH_IP        which Tapo bulb flashes on an open
#   DOOR_FLASH_HUE, DOOR_FLASH_SATURATION, DOOR_FLASH_BRIGHTNESS, DOOR_FLASH_MS
#   DOOR_QUIET_FROM, DOOR_QUIET_TO
#   DOOR_POLL_MS         how often to poll Supabase. Defaults to 60000
